value calls value.replace(...) and so needs a str. file.name is a str (ModelFile name). The only non-test remove_file caller, controller.py:589, passes diff.old_file.name, also a str. No path passes None or a non-str, so the change adds no new AttributeError risk.","Ordering: the sanitized debug log still runs before the existence check and ModelError raise, so control flow and exception behavior match the old code. ModelError messages contain no filename, so they need no sanitization.","Schema/migration: none. Persistence: none. This affects only the debug-level log output format: CR/LF become literal \\r/\\n and other C0 characters and DEL become \\xHH. Any log-scraping tooling that matched raw filenames containing control characters would see escaped text. This is the intended outcome of the CWE-117 work and only affects pathological filenames.","Blast radius: limited to one module (model.py), at debug log level only. The RED tests in commit 7035477 (test_model.py) cover the 3 sites.","Verdict: shippable as-is. The only note is a low-confidence, non-blocking point about sanitizing eagerly when DEBUG is off."]}
